// @expect-error A 'char' is a code point and never converts to 'double' on its own. Add 'as double' after the literal to use its code point as a 'double'.
// A code point is a name for a character, not a measurement, so letting it drift into a
// floating-point number would turn a mistake into 65.0 rather than reporting it.
main() -> int {
    double code = 'A';
    return code > 0.0 ? 0 : 1;
}
